            "inlines": [
              {
                "kind": "text",
                "value": "While the community tests Asciidoctor on a variety of Linux distributions, it’s only officially tested on Ubuntu and Fedora."
              }
            ],
            "roles": [],
            "title": null
          }
        ],
        "context": "section",
        "id": "_operating_systems",
        "level": 1,
        "roles": [],
        "title": [
          {
            "kind": "text",
            "value": "Operating systems"
          }
        ]
      },
      {
        "blocks": [
          {
            "context": "paragraph",
            "id": null,
            "inlines": [
              {
                "kind": "text",
                "value": "Asciidoctor assumes you’re using UTF-8 encoding. To minimize encoding problems, make sure the default encoding of your system is set to UTF-8."
              }
            ],
            "roles": [],
            "title": null
          },
          {
            "context": "paragraph",
            "id": null,
            "inlines": [
              {
                "kind": "text",
                "value": "If you’re using a non-English Windows environment, you may bump into an "
              },
              {
                "id": null,
                "inlines": [
                  {
                    "kind": "text",
                    "value": "Encoding::UndefinedConversionError"
                  }
                ],
                "kind": "monospace",
                "roles": []
              },
              {
                "kind": "text",
                "value": " when invoking Asciidoctor. To solve this issue, we recommend overriding the default external and internal character encodings to "
              },
              {
                "id": null,
                "inlines": [
                  {
                    "kind": "text",
                    "value": "utf-8"
                  }
                ],
                "kind": "monospace",
                "roles": []
              },
              {
                "kind": "text",
                "value": ". You can do so by setting the "
              },
              {
                "id": null,
                "inlines": [
                  {
                    "kind": "text",
                    "value": "RUBYOPT"
                  }
                ],
                "kind": "monospace",
                "roles": []
              },
              {
                "kind": "text",
                "value": " environment variable as follows:"
              }
            ],
            "roles": [],
            "title": null
          },
          {
            "context": "literal",
            "id": null,
            "inlines": [
              {
                "kind": "text",
                "value": "RUBYOPT=\"-E utf-8:utf-8\""
              }
            ],
            "language": null,
            "roles": [],
            "title": null
          },
          {
            "context": "paragraph",
            "id": null,
            "inlines": [
              {
                "kind": "text",
                "value": "Once you make this change, all your Unicode headaches should be behind you."
              }
            ],
            "roles": [],
            "title": null
          },
          {
            "context": "paragraph",
            "id": null,
            "inlines": [
              {
                "kind": "text",
                "value": "If you’re using an IDE like Eclipse, make sure you set the encoding to UTF-8 there as well. Asciidoctor is optimized to work with UTF-8 as the default encoding."
              }
            ],
            "roles": [],
            "title": null
          }
        ],
